   }
  },
  "e4189fec-83c2-4000-9e17-3c8cd6deddf8": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Cape Grim – CH₄ and N₂O (panel b)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     16074387.638258236,
     -4987315.736142753,
     16139246.60749927,
     -4944076.4233153965
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Cape Grim – CH₄ and N₂O (panel b)",
     "markdown": "🔵 **ONLINE** – published, link only (not re-hosted here)\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Station** | CSIRO / Bureau of Meteorology baseline station, member of **AGAGE** |\n| **In the CEDA Fig 2.5 file** | `AGAGE_CH4` (1987–), `AGAGE_N2O` (1979–), `CSIRO_CH4`, `CSIRO_N2O` (1992–), `UCI_CH4` (1978–) |\n| **2019 global means** | CH₄ ≈ 1867 ppb · N₂O ≈ 332 ppb |\n| **Links** | [csiro.au/greenhouse-gases](https://www.csiro.au/greenhouse-gases) · [agage.mit.edu](https://agage.mit.edu/) |\n\n➡ **Next** – Exeter and the surface-temperature record.",
     "image": ""
    },
