    }
   }
  },
  "68b504ce-7e10-40ea-afbe-bfdb2541de85": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Exeter – the surface temperature record (panels c, d)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -419153.39563635003,
     6551524.861095589,
     -354294.42639531475,
     6594764.173922945
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Exeter – the surface temperature record (panels c, d)",
     "markdown": "🟢 **AVAILABLE** – copy in this project, loaded live from the archive when online\n\n**HadCRUT5** (Met Office Hadley Centre / UEA) is one of four datasets averaged into the AR6 assessed global temperature.\nCEDA publishes that four-dataset table as an *input data* record:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Record** | WGI Ch.2 – *Input data for Figure 2.11* (v20220428) |\n| **DOI** | [10.5285/033cd690…](https://doi.org/10.5285/033cd690801741c9bc745b8da55faef4) |\n| **File** | `Figure_2_11c-lower_panel.csv` – HadCRUT, NOAA, Berkeley, Kadow 1850–2020 + decadal means |\n| **Also in record** | HadCRUT trend and significance grids 1900–1980 / 1981–2020 |\n| **In project** | `data/input/wgi_ch2_fig2_11_input/` |\n\nOther inputs cited here: **HadCRUT4.6** (basis of panel d, 1.06 °C) and the **PAGES 2k** reconstruction (1–2000 CE).\n\n➡ **Next** – Ispra and the emissions inventory.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "36ed502d-506c-485c-9a08-ecb346aa72f7": {
